# Wire protocol

You are editing files that define the contract between the TypeScript
extension and the Go agent. Changes here must be symmetric.

## Rules

1. Every message type in `src/shared/protocol.ts` must have a matching shape
   on the Go side (struct or `map[string]any` accessed consistently).
2. When adding a method, register handlers on both sides in the same change.
3. Use LSP-style `Content-Length` framing. Do not introduce newline-delimited
   JSON or any other framing.
4. Method naming uses dot namespaces: `task.*`, `message.*`, `tool.*`, `system.*`.
5. Distinguish requests (have `id`, expect response) from notifications (no `id`).
   Document the distinction in `CLAUDE.md` when adding a method.

## Debugging desync

If the codec gets stuck, the cause is almost always unframed bytes on the
channel. Check for stray `fmt.Print*` to stdout in Go code — all logs must
go to stderr.
